5.4 Web Framework and Frontend Technologies Used
5.4.1 Flask (Python Web Framework)
Introduction to Flask:
Flask is a lightweight, flexible Python web framework designed for building scalable web applications with minimal boilerplate while maintaining full control over architecture.

Why Flask Was Chosen for AURA:

Simplicity: Clean, readable code structure for rapid development
Modularity: Easy separation of routes, services, and models for maintainability
Extensibility: Seamless integration with Flask-SocketIO for real-time communication
Production-Ready: Proven in educational institutions globally; easy to monitor and debug
Lightweight: Lower resource footprint compared to FastAPI, ideal for educational deployments
MongoDB Integration: Direct support via Flask-MongoEngine and PyMongo
